Lemma 6.64. Let X be regular. Then, TFAE: Every open covering U of X
has a refinement that is:
  1. a locally finite open cover;
  2. A countably locally finite open cover, i.e., it can be written as a countable
     union of locally finite collections;
  3. a locally finite cover;
  4. a locally finite closed cover.

